      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ASK YOUR MOTHER (1) brings the right profile to resume a strong winning chance, having been sent out favourite when sixth at Pakenham Synthetic before the break after being slow to begin. His earlier fourth at the same venue was sound enough, and his record of three placings from five starts in the past 12 months suggests he has the consistency to be highly competitive in this maiden. BE BRIEF (2) is lightly raced and gets first-time blinkers after failing to quicken as a well-supported favourite at Balaklava, with his debut fifth at Morphettville showing enough to keep him firmly in the mix. PIERRE LE QUILL (5) has the recent placing pattern, finishing second at Mildura then third at Echuca, and the blinkers plus Jarrod Todd give him solid claims if the 1200m is suitable. PRINCE OF SPARTA (6) was only beaten half a length at this track 10 days ago and backs up from a well-supported second, although he still has to convert that into a maiden win.",
